### Run these in IntelliJ, top to bottom: open this file and click the green ▶ next to each request.
### Start the app first. The H2 database is empty on every start.
### The login requests save their token, so later requests can use {{teacher}} / {{student}}.

### 1. Register a teacher and a student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "teacher@hvl.no", "name": "Tina Teacher", "password": "secret-password"}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "student@hvl.no", "name": "Sam Student", "password": "secret-password"}

### 2. Log in as both (saves the tokens)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "teacher@hvl.no", "password": "secret-password"}

> {% client.global.set("teacher", response.body.accessToken); %}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "student@hvl.no", "password": "secret-password"}

> {% client.global.set("student", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 3. Teacher creates course 1 (and becomes its teacher)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "DAT250", "description": "Software technologies", "semester": "Autumn 2026"}

### 4. Teacher invites the student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/enrollments
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "student@hvl.no", "role": "STUDENT"}

### 5. Modules
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/modules
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Week 1: Introduction"}

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/modules
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}

### 6. Content: a page, and an assignment (id 2) worth 10 points
POST http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/pages
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Welcome", "body": "# Welcome to DAT250"}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Hand-in 1", "description": "Upload your report", "deadline": "2099-01-01T00:00:00Z", "maxPoints": 10}

### 7. The student sees the module's (visible) contents
GET http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/contents
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}

### 8. The student hands in (submission 1)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/contents/2/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"answer": "https://git.app.uib.no/sam/hand-in-1"}

### 9. The student tries to grade -> 403 Forbidden
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/submissions/1/grade
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"points": 10}

### 10. The teacher grades
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/submissions/1/grade
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"points": 9, "feedback": "Clear and well structured"}

### 11. Gradebook (teachers only)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/gradebook
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}

### 12. The student's own grades (hidden until published)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/my-grades
Authorization: Bearer {{student}}

### 13. Publish the grades, then run 12 again
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/contents/2/grades-published
Authorization: Bearer {{teacher}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"published": true}

### 14. No token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses
